{"card": {"id": "quantum_golay", "kind": "family", "identity": {"canonical_name": "Quantum Golay code", "variant": "fixed binary CSS block", "aliases": ["binary quantum Golay code"]}, "presentation": {"orienting_view": {"status": "available", "kind": "stabilizer-incidence"}, "guided_tour": {"status": "not-required", "until_tier": "T3"}}, "eczoo": {"status": "mapped", "zoo_id": "qubit_golay", "classification": "exact-family", "source": {"repository_url": "https://github.com/errorcorrectionzoo/eczoo_data", "commit": "b2437d9e2dc09284e04c66ef72ee81b7ed7bd129", "retrieved_on": "2026-08-05", "path": "codes/quantum/qubits/stabilizer/magic/qubit_golay.yml", "sha256": "ecc6b730a7beae19509246210d76d05085ac196158f69e30747aca6129da7805", "page_url": "https://errorcorrectionzoo.org/c/qubit_golay", "blob_url": "https://github.com/errorcorrectionzoo/eczoo_data/blob/b2437d9e2dc09284e04c66ef72ee81b7ed7bd129/codes/quantum/qubits/stabilizer/magic/qubit_golay.yml"}}, "description": "A fixed binary CSS stabilizer block built from the self-orthogonal subcode of the classical binary Golay code. The same declared binary check space is used in the X and Z sectors, so the executable matrix determines the protected quotient without introducing a spatial lattice. This card denotes the quantum block, not the classical Golay code, a qutrit analogue, or the wider quadratic-residue construction.", "views": [{"rung": "R1", "type": "golay-css-matrix", "description": "The constructor takes the even rows of the primary paper's displayed Golay matrix as one ordered binary block and duplicates that block into pure-X and pure-Z stabilizers. Its odd all-one row supplies a declared logical pair, while exact finite enumeration checks the first nontrivial normalizer weight.", "origin": {"kind": "canonical"}, "refs": ["sullivan2024golay", "steane1996simple"]}], "categories": [{"id": "css", "origin": {"kind": "verified"}}], "refs": ["steane1996simple", "sullivan2024golay"], "params": {}, "visual_instance": "g